## WHAT THIS APP IS — read this first, every time

**Coalition H.U.D is Sawyer's entire eBay workflow in a heads-up display — from sifting a
pile of cards, toys, electronics or sealed product, all the way to the package arriving at
the customer's doorstep.** It replaces roughly 17 separate softwares and sites with one.

It is NOT a scan-identify-list tool. That is one feature inside it. Every time this gets
reduced to "scan → identify → list," it is wrong, and Sawyer has corrected it repeatedly.

The surfaces, and what each one is:

- **Scouter** — mobile intake ONLY. Camera, barcode, photo dump. Capture on the go, then
  move to desktop. **Scouter does not list.** It is the front door, not the app.
- **Spaces** — collection/storage tracker built on real photos of his real bins. Physical
  nesting mirrored digitally: outer tote → pull-out fridge bins → Connect Kinetic holders →
  cards / Goat mini team bags. Click a space and it zooms forward into the next level.
  Floating interactive bins. Listed bins and unlisted/staged bins are different things.
- **Spine** — the structured glowing constellation. Items float on a line and move down it
  stage by stage until listed, then file into their bins. Click = half-zoom info card, not
  full screen. **Structured constellation, never the molecule chaos Base44 produced.**
- **Channels** — eBay live, plus Double Holo, Misprint, Shopify.
- **Shipping** — same constellation path: dropoff → scan → in transit → doorstep.
- **Listing engine** — identify, titles, descriptions, pricing, templates. This is the part
  that replaces TCGAutomate.

Two things drive the whole build:

1. **Don't lose photos.** Ever, at any stage.
2. **He can see the whole line move.** That is what "heads-up display" means here.

Business reality: TCGAutomate Pro costs $40/month and locks inventory sync behind the top
tier. This app replacing it is a real bill going away, not a nice-to-have. But that is the
*motivation*, not the scope. The scope is the whole workflow above.

